\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Now let us see Thy beauty, Lord,
\par As we have seen before;
\par And by Thy beauty quicken us
\par To love Thee and adore.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. 'Tis easy when with simple mind
\par Thy loveliness we see;
\par To consecrate ourselves afresh
\par To duty and to Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Our every feverish mood is cooled,
\par And gone is every load,
\par When we can lose the love of self,
\par And find the love of God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. 'Tis by Thy loveliness we're won
\par To home and Thee again,
\par And as we are Thy children true
\par We are more truly men.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Lord, it is coming to ourselves
\par When thus we come to Thee;
\par The bondage of Thy loveliness
\par Is perfect liberty.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. So now we come to ask again
\par What Thou hast often given,
\par The vision of that loveliness
\par Which is the life of heaven.\f1 
\par 
\par }

